Manifest.toml
# ...except the generator's: gen/generate.jl's output is checked in and verified
# byte-for-byte, so the whole formatter dependency tree has to be pinned.
!gen/Manifest.toml
# ...and the examples': pinning the example stack stops a Genie upgrade
# reddening a pull request. The weekly drift job resolves without it, on
# purpose.
!examples/Manifest.toml
# Documenter's output. Regenerated by every `docs/make.jl`.
docs/build/
# Screenshots, traces and videos the examples write.
examples/output/
*.png
.CondaPkg/
# Traces, video and PDF written by the artifact tests. Binaries, and
# regenerated on every run — never worth committing.
artifacts/
# The browser cache, when PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH points into the checkout —
# which is what the README's CI recipe and CI.yml both do. Several hundred
# megabytes of downloaded browser, one `git add -A` away from being committed.
.playwright/
